  "details": "I’m 17 and have been part of VRChat since 2019, and I believe it’s time we rethink the restrictions placed on changing our usernames.\n\nVRChat has always stood for self-expression, individuality, and giving people the freedom to discover and represent who they are — including its open support for the LGBTQ+ community. Our identities can change, and the way we represent ourselves should be allowed to change with them.\n\nA 30–90 day restriction works against that freedom. We should be trusted to choose our names and change them when we feel they no longer represent us. This isn’t about abusing the system — it’s about giving people the same freedom of expression that VRChat has always championed.\n\nLet people represent themselves freely. Let people change. Let VRChat lead by example.",
